---
// /power: two signals for enterprise facilities already running. Figures live in src/lib/power.ts.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SourceMark from '../../components/SourceMark.astro';
import { pjm, eiaPrices, eiaStates, eiaReleased, pct, cents } from '../../lib/power';

const sectors = ['Commercial', 'Industrial'] as const;
const rows = [
  ...eiaStates.map((name) => ({ name, national: false, cells: sectors.map((s) => eiaPrices.sectors[s].states[name]) })),
  { name: 'U.S. average', national: true, cells: sectors.map((s) => ({ ...eiaPrices.sectors[s].us, rank_by_change: null })) },
];
const count = eiaPrices.sectors.Commercial.statesCounted;
---
<Base title="Power" description="Grid supply and electricity cost for enterprise data centers already in operation, with the source behind every figure.">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Power</h1>
      <p class="lede">Grid supply and electricity cost for facilities already running: what changed, what the figure measures, and the question it raises for your site.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="panel panel-reading prose">

      <!-- Signal 1: PJM capacity and reserves -->
      <section class="signal" id="pjm-capacity">
        <p class="sig-k">Grid supply &middot; PJM region, including Virginia and Ohio</p>
        <h2>The PJM grid secured less capacity than its reliability requirement for 2028/29</h2>
        <p class="facts"><strong>Delivery year:</strong> {pjm.deliveryYear} &middot; <strong>Auction results:</strong> {pjm.reportDate} &middot; <strong>Second auction in a row below requirement</strong></p>

        <ul class="stats">
          <li><span class="stat-n">{pjm.shortfallMw} MW</span><span class="stat-l">below PJM's reliability requirement (unforced capacity). Previous auction: {pjm.priorShortfallMw} MW.</span></li>
          <li><span class="stat-n">{pjm.totalReserveMargin}</span><span class="stat-l">estimated total reserve margin, against a {pjm.targetReserveMargin} target</span></li>
          <li><span class="stat-n">{pjm.clearingPrice}</span><span class="stat-l">per MW-day, the auction's price cap</span></li>
        </ul>

        <p>PJM runs this auction to secure enough generation, and demand that can be reduced, for a future year.
          For 2028/29 it secured {pjm.procuredMw} MW of unforced capacity, a rating that discounts each resource
          for how reliably it can deliver. That was {pjm.shortfallMw} MW short of the {pjm.requirementMw} MW
          requirement. PJM says the shortfall "does not necessarily mean that the PJM system will be unable to
          serve load reliably", but that it "would have to operate with slimmer reserves and greater level of risk."</p>

        <p><strong>Two reserve margins appear in the report.</strong> {pjm.totalReserveMargin} is PJM's estimate for
          the whole region, counting capacity bought in the auction and capacity that some utilities commit from their
          own resources. {pjm.auctionReserveMargin} counts the auction alone. Both are below the {pjm.targetReserveMargin}
          target, which PJM sets to hold the expected loss of load to one day in ten years.</p>

        <p>This is the second auction in a row to clear more than one percentage point below that target. Under
          PJM's current rules, a third would require a separate backstop auction. PJM says it is working on changes
          to those rules.</p>

        <h3>Clearing price, $ per MW-day</h3>
        <div class="tbl-wrap wide-only">
          <table class="tbl">
            <thead><tr>{pjm.priceHistory.map((p) => <th scope="col">{p.year}</th>)}</tr></thead>
            <tbody><tr>{pjm.priceHistory.map((p) => <td>{p.price}</td>)}</tr></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <table class="tbl narrow-only">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col" class="l">Delivery year</th><th scope="col">$ per MW-day</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{pjm.priceHistory.map((p) => <tr><th scope="row" class="l">{p.year}</th><td>{p.price}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="small">Region-wide prices for each delivery year, as listed in PJM's 2028/29 report. The 2027/28 and
          2028/29 auctions both cleared at their price caps.</p>

        <div class="arith">
          <p><strong>{pjm.perMwYear} per MW-year is arithmetic, not a bill estimate.</strong> It is the 2028/29
            wholesale clearing price ({pjm.clearingPrice} per MW-day of unforced capacity) multiplied by 365 days.
            PJM notes that its auction totals do not equal the cost to customers, because customers whose supply is
            hedged are not exposed to the clearing price. What a facility pays depends on its capacity obligation
            and its supply arrangement.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ask">
          <p class="ask-q">The question for an existing facility in PJM:<br />
            <strong>How is my capacity obligation determined, and could managing load at the relevant peak times affect it?</strong></p>
          <p>The answer depends on how you buy power: default service from your utility, a contract with a competitive
            supplier, or a utility that supplies its own capacity. It also depends on how your contract treats capacity
            cost: passed through, fixed, or bundled into the price. Your utility or supplier can tell you how the
            obligation is set, whether particular peak hours matter, when it is recalculated, and whether a change
            would reach your bill.</p>
        </div>

        <p class="src"><SourceMark type="G" /><span>PJM Interconnection, <a href={pjm.reportUrl}>{pjm.reportTitle}</a> (PDF),
          {pjm.reportDate}, pages 3&ndash;5.</span></p>
      </section>

      <!-- Signal 2: EIA commercial and industrial averages -->
      <section class="signal" id="electricity-prices">
        <p class="sig-k">Electricity cost &middot; updated monthly</p>
        <h2>Average electricity prices, {eiaPrices.periodCurrent}</h2>
        <p class="facts"><strong>Data through:</strong> {eiaPrices.dataThrough} &middot; <strong>Released:</strong> {eiaReleased}
          &middot; <strong>Status:</strong> preliminary</p>

        <div class="tbl-wrap wide-only">
          <table class="tbl tbl-eia">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col" rowspan="2" class="l">Cents per kWh</th>
                <th scope="colgroup" colspan="3">Commercial</th>
                <th scope="colgroup" colspan="3">Industrial</th>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">2026</th><th scope="col">vs 2025</th><th scope="col">Rank</th>
                <th scope="col">2026</th><th scope="col">vs 2025</th><th scope="col">Rank</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {rows.map((r) => (
                <tr class={r.national ? 'nat' : undefined}>
                  <th scope="row" class="l">{r.name}</th>
                  {r.cells.map((c) => (
                    <>
                      <td>{cents(c.current)}</td>
                      <td>{pct(c.change_pct)}</td>
                      <td>{c.rank_by_change ?? '—'}</td>
                    </>
                  ))}
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        {sectors.map((sector, i) => (
          <table class="tbl narrow-only tbl-sector">
            <caption>{sector} customers, cents per kWh</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col" class="l">State</th><th scope="col">2026</th><th scope="col">vs 2025</th><th scope="col">Rank</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {rows.map((r) => (
                <tr class={r.national ? 'nat' : undefined}>
                  <th scope="row" class="l">{r.name}</th>
                  <td>{cents(r.cells[i].current)}</td>
                  <td>{pct(r.cells[i].change_pct)}</td>
                  <td>{r.cells[i].rank_by_change ?? '—'}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        ))}
        <p class="small">Change compares {eiaPrices.periodCurrent} with {eiaPrices.periodPrior}. Rank is by size of
          change among {count} jurisdictions (the 50 states and DC), where 1 is the largest increase. Across all {count},
          the median change was {pct(eiaPrices.sectors.Commercial.medianStateChangePct)} for commercial customers and
          {pct(eiaPrices.sectors.Industrial.medianStateChangePct)} for industrial. The four states shown are DCU's
          launch coverage, not a selection by result.</p>

        <div class="note">
          <p><strong>Not your facility's tariff.</strong> These are statewide averages across all commercial or all
            industrial customers, as estimated by EIA. They are not the rate any one facility pays, and they do not
            explain why prices moved. Depending on the utility, a 1&ndash;10 MW site may be billed on a commercial or
            an industrial rate schedule, which is why both are shown.</p>
        </div>

        <p class="src"><SourceMark type="G" /><span>U.S. Energy Information Administration, <a href={eiaPrices.url}>{eiaPrices.publication},
          {eiaPrices.table}</a>, data for {eiaPrices.dataThrough}, released {eiaReleased}. Preliminary estimates, revised in later editions.</span></p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .signal + .signal { margin-top: 2.2em; padding-top: 1.6em; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .sig-k { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: .3em !important; }
  .signal h2 { font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0 0 .5em; padding: 0; border: 0; }
  .signal h3 { font-size: 15px; margin: 1.4em 0 .5em; }
  .facts { font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-2); background: var(--page); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 5px; padding: 8px 12px; }
  .facts strong { color: var(--ink); }

  .stats { list-style: none; padding: 0 !important; display: grid; gap: 10px; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); margin: 1.1em 0 1.2em !important; }
  .stats li { margin: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 14px; }
  .stat-n { display: block; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; letter-spacing: -.3px; }
  .stat-l { display: block; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink-2); margin-top: 2px; }

  .tbl-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0 0 .6em; }
  .tbl { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 14.5px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; margin: 0 !important; }
  .tbl th, .tbl td { padding: 7px 10px; text-align: right; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2); white-space: nowrap; }
  .tbl thead th { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-2); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .tbl .l { text-align: left; }
  .tbl tbody th { font-weight: 500; }
  .tbl-eia thead tr:first-child th:not(.l) { text-align: center; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
  .tbl-eia tbody td:nth-child(4), .tbl-eia thead tr:last-child th:nth-child(3) { border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .tbl .nat th, .tbl .nat td { font-weight: 600; background: var(--page); }
  .tbl caption { caption-side: top; text-align: left; font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); padding: 0 0 4px; }
  .tbl-sector + .tbl-sector { margin-top: 1em !important; }
  .narrow-only { margin-bottom: .6em !important; }
  .wide-only { display: none; }
  .small { font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-2); }

  .arith, .note { background: var(--amber-bg); border: 1px solid var(--amber-ln); border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 15px; margin: 1.1em 0; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .arith p, .note p { margin: 0; }
  .ask { border-left: 3px solid var(--blue); background: var(--blue-lt); border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0; padding: 13px 16px; margin: 1.1em 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .ask p:last-child { margin: 0; }
  .ask-q { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .ask-q strong { color: var(--ink); font-size: 16.5px; }

  .src { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 1em; }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .wide-only { display: block; }
    .narrow-only { display: none; }
    .stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }
</style>
